  "id": "helping-professions",
  "term": "helping professions",
  "definition": "Helping professions are jobs in human services where workers support people facing major hardship, crisis, distress, or suffering. Because this work often involves ongoing exposure to clients’ painful circumstances and complex needs, these workers can be especially vulnerable to stress and burnout.",
